title: 'pallet-referenda: fix referendum stranded when the track queue is full'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes a bug in `pallet-referenda` where a referendum could be permanently stranded
    when its track queue is full. `ready_for_deciding` set `in_queue = true`
    unconditionally even when `insert_sorted_by_key` did not insert the item (it sorted
    beyond the `MaxQueued` bound), so the referendum was flagged as queued while absent
    from `TrackQueue` - never nudged into deciding and skipped by the undeciding timeout.
    `in_queue` is now derived from the actual insertion result, and when the queue is full
    a wake-up is scheduled at the undeciding timeout so the referendum begins deciding (if
    a slot has freed) or times out, instead of being stranded with its decision deposit
    locked.
crates:
- name: pallet-referenda
  bump: patch
